   those licences give you in that software.

5. No warranty. The builds are provided "as is", without warranty of any
   kind, express or implied, including the warranties of merchantability,
   fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. In no event shall
   the authors be liable for any claim, damages or other liability arising
   from the builds or their use, to the extent the applicable law allows.

6. Later releases may come under other terms, an open-source licence among
   them. These terms apply to the builds published with them.
